  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Well, overall, better. The main thing is the hot flushes. Before the patch I was having about eight a day, and now I'm down to about three a day.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:44",
      "end_timestamp": "01:01",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Eight down to three. That's a big change. How would you describe them now, compared to before?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:02",
      "end_timestamp": "01:11",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Fine. It's the combined patch, estradiol and norethisterone. 50 micrograms. I change it twice a week, Monday and Thursday, without fail.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:38",
      "end_timestamp": "01:50",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, regularly. Well... that's what I'd like to say. Honestly, looking at the diary, there are three Thursdays last month where I wrote 'forgot'. I changed it on Friday instead.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:01",
      "end_timestamp": "02:15",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, about three late changes last month, and perhaps a couple the month before. I can't give you the exact number, I only started marking it after the first month.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:30",
      "end_timestamp": "02:46",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Good. Any bleeding or spotting since you began? Anything like that?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:36",
      "end_timestamp": "03:42",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Nothing unexpected. A light bleed in the first month, which you said to expect. Nothing since.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:44",
      "end_timestamp": "03:54",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Only the low bone density, osteopenia, they called it, found on my scan two years ago. And I get migraines occasionally.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:06",
      "end_timestamp": "04:15",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Thank you. Let me take your measurements while we talk. Blood pressure is 118 over 74.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:27",
      "end_timestamp": "04:34",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And your weight is 66 kilograms, which is the same as last time, I see.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:37",
      "end_timestamp": "04:46",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any trouble with your heart lately, chest pain, palpitations, or shortness of breath on the stairs?",
      "start_timestamp": "04:56",
      "end_timestamp": "05:05",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "No, nothing. My heart feels normal. I climbed the stairs at the lab four times yesterday without a problem.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:07",
      "end_timestamp": "05:18",
      "supports": [
        "review_of_systems[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Your chest is clear. Now let me check your calves, since you're on estrogen. They're soft and not tender, with no swelling.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:49",
      "end_timestamp": "06:00",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]",
        "physical_examination[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "A few late changes won't harm you, but a steady level keeps the flushes down. Could you set a reminder on your phone for Thursday afternoons?",
      "start_timestamp": "07:24",
      "end_timestamp": "07:36",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, I'll set a recurring alarm for two o'clock, and I'll keep a spare patch in my bag at the lab.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:39",
      "end_timestamp": "07:48",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That sounds perfect. Based on your diary, this looks like menopausal flushes that are responding well to the patch.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:50",
      "end_timestamp": "07:59",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes. I'd like to see you again in three months, to check your blood pressure and how things are going.",
      "start_timestamp": "08:10",
      "end_timestamp": "08:21",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]",
        "follow_up[0]"
      ]
